# Line endings, pinned.
#
# With no file here, git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and
# checks every file it guesses is text out with CRLF. That is how
# `serve::tests::apply_arms_match_the_table` failed the first time the
# suite was ever run on Windows: it reads its own source with include_str!
# and splits on "\n}\n", which a CRLF checkout can never match, so the
# guard reported "apply_setting has no recognisable end" instead of
# reporting drift. Anything that hashes, embeds or parses our own source
# has the same exposure, so the byte stream is one canonical thing on
# every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Test fixtures are BYTE-EXACT and must never be line-ending converted,
# whatever git's text/binary heuristic guesses about them.
#
# Two of these have no NUL in the first 8000 bytes, so git reads them as
# ordinary text and the rule above would silently rewrite them:
# `vendor/rars/tests/fixtures/rar13/README` (49 CRLF pairs) and
# `vendor/rars/tests/fixtures/rar15_40/ppmd/escape_64k.bin` (1337 of
# them) - the second is a PPMd corpus where every byte is the thing under
# test. `-text` also stops today's Windows checkout injecting 21 CRs into
# `crates/nzbkit/testdata/spot/free.pt.over.tsv`, a latin-1 Spotnet
# fixture that git likewise reads as text.
crates/nzbkit/testdata/**          -text
crates/nzbkit/tests/fixtures/**    -text
vendor/rars/tests/fixtures/**      -text

# Same exposure, one directory over: `crates/nzbkit/fuzz/seeds/**` holds
# committed corpus entries and crash repros for the cargo-fuzz targets,
# several of them CRLF yEnc control-line framing (the `=y` protocol is
# CRLF-terminated) with no NUL early enough to trip git's binary
# heuristic - `git add` on this Mac warned it would silently replace
# their CRLF with LF on the very commit that added them (27 Aug 2026,
# the post-v1.2.4 fuzz campaign), which is the exact corruption the rule
# above exists to prevent, just undiscovered here because nothing had
# committed a CRLF-bearing seed under this directory before. It was
# never actually mangled - the `-text` below landed before the commit -
# but the pre-existing `seeds/rar_recovery_scan/` and `seeds/rar_name_probe/`
# corpora were exposed to the identical risk on any checkout that
# resolves `text=auto` differently (a Windows clone with
# `core.autocrlf=true` in particular) for however long they have been
# committed; this rule closes that retroactively as well as prospectively.
crates/nzbkit/fuzz/seeds/**        -text

# cmd.exe's own format. `Start nzbfast.bat` has labels and a `goto` out of
# a `for` block, which is the construct where an LF-only batch file misfires
# on some cmd.exe versions, so this is pinned CRLF rather than left to the
# default above. `packaging/windows/installer.iss` is deliberately NOT
# here: Inno Setup reads LF, and LF is what the shipping installer has
# been built from all along.
#
# The `build.cmd` that packaging/windows/make-installer.sh sends to the
# build box is unaffected either way - that file is generated at run time
# with literal \r\n and scp'd from a temp path, so it is never in git.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# The claims ledger is append-only JSONL merged by hand on every push
# race (177 append-append conflicts in six hours on one box's view of
# origin/main, measured 31 Aug 2026) - every one of them a lane
# hand-resolving two sides that each only appended lines. Git's built-in
# union driver auto-resolves exactly that shape: verified in a throwaway
# repo where two branches each append a different record to the file's
# end. It needs no per-clone config, being a built-in rather than a
# custom `merge.*.driver`, so this one line reaches the whole fleet.
# `tools/claims.py`'s reducer already sorts by each record's own `ts`
# (see `_ev_key`'s docstring) rather than by file position, and already
# tolerates a duplicated record, so union's reordering and the rare
# byte-identical duplicate it can produce were both true before this
# line and needed no change here. This is a toil and risk fix, not a
# response to data loss: two independent audits (this line's own claim,
# and `claims-ledger-superset-gate`'s 2,040-commit / 1,331-record sweep)
# found zero genuine drops from hand-resolving these conflicts.
research/CLAIMS.jsonl merge=union
